It says, verse 5,

222
00:16:26,580 --> 00:16:36,760
We've all heard of forest fires.

223
00:16:36,760 --> 00:16:38,640
There have been a lot recently.

224
00:16:38,640 --> 00:16:42,200
So we can visualize this pretty easily.

225
00:16:42,200 --> 00:16:45,680
I've never seen one in person, but I've seen a lot on TV.

226
00:16:45,680 --> 00:16:54,300
And here's a picture of a forest set on fire and the power of that, the lives that that takes.

227
00:16:54,880 --> 00:17:03,380
I wanted to show you a side-by-side of a before and after picture of a fire that took place in Santa Rosa, California in October 2017.

228
00:17:03,380 --> 00:17:06,340
On this side, you see the before.

229
00:17:06,340 --> 00:17:09,700
The houses, how everything looked, the aerial view.

230
00:17:09,700 --> 00:17:12,060
And then on this side, you see the after.

231
00:17:12,780 --> 00:17:25,860
And James' point is a spark, a single word, a single statement can grow and grow and grow to destroy your life or someone else's life.

232
00:17:25,860 --> 00:17:28,540
This specific one makes me think of gossip.

233
00:17:28,540 --> 00:17:33,820
You start talking about something and the word grows and grows.

234
00:17:33,820 --> 00:17:36,880
You put something on social media and it grows and grows.

235
00:17:37,220 --> 00:17:41,980
And before you know it, complete and utter destruction has occurred.

236
00:17:41,980 --> 00:17:48,520
This fire burned more than 36,810 acres, killed over 22 people.

237
00:17:48,520 --> 00:17:49,240
They say at least.

238
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:50,200
I'm not sure how that works.

239
00:17:50,200 --> 00:17:53,980
But destroyed 5,643 structures.

240
00:17:53,980 --> 00:17:59,320
And it started because of a spark in an electric unit in a private home.

241
00:17:59,880 --> 00:18:02,080
One spark did all of that.

242
00:18:02,080 --> 00:18:07,120
What can one word do or a few words do?

243
00:18:07,120 --> 00:18:08,420
Either it's a positive or negative.

244
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:13,120
And the reality is they can rebuild this, but it will never be what it was.

245
00:18:13,120 --> 00:18:17,420
And people who have spoken negatively into your life can rebuild.

246
00:18:17,420 --> 00:18:25,640
You can rebuild what they have done, but there will always be a part of you, unfortunately, that will remember that.

247
00:18:25,800 --> 00:18:28,480
And we'll fully be able to restore that.

248
00:18:28,480 --> 00:18:36,380
My husband, in his high school football days, had a lot of coaches that spoke really positively.

249
00:18:36,380 --> 00:18:41,940
But he always remembers that one coach that spoke negatively to him.

250
00:18:41,940 --> 00:18:44,460
As a grown adult, he still remembers the exact words.

251
00:18:44,460 --> 00:18:47,280
That is what our words are capable of.

252
00:18:47,280 --> 00:18:49,720
And God wants us to realize that.

253
00:18:50,460 --> 00:18:55,140
So then we go to verse 6, continuing to talk about this fire.

254
00:18:55,140 --> 00:18:59,920
The tongue is also a fire, a world of evil among the parts of the body.

255
00:18:59,920 --> 00:19:04,160
It corrupts the whole body, sets the whole course of one's life on fire.

256
00:19:04,160 --> 00:19:06,920
And it itself is set on fire by hell.

257
00:19:06,920 --> 00:19:08,160
These are strong words.

258
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:12,160
But the bottom line is, is Satan loves the power of our words.

259
00:19:12,160 --> 00:19:15,080
He wants you and I to believe that our words don't hold power.

260
00:19:15,080 --> 00:19:18,220
Because then we can destroy someone's life and not realize we're doing it.

261
00:19:18,220 --> 00:19:24,000
He would love for nothing else than for us to use our words unwisely and not to think before we speak.

262
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:26,580
And destroy life after life after life.

263
00:19:26,580 --> 00:19:30,800
Then, when we realize we've destroyed all of those lives, we're so far from God.

264
00:19:30,800 --> 00:19:34,220
We're so ashamed of what we've done that we don't want to go back to God.

265
00:19:34,220 --> 00:19:35,640
And again, Satan wins.

266
00:19:35,640 --> 00:19:41,680
So, that's why God talks so much about the power of our words in the Bible.

267
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:45,660
Because he doesn't want Satan to gain that foothold in our lives.

268
00:19:45,660 --> 00:19:52,660
Verse 7 says, all kinds of animals, birds, reptiles, and sea creatures are being tamed and have been tamed by mankind.

269
00:19:52,660 --> 00:19:55,520
Just a footnote, they have never met my three dogs.

270
00:19:55,520 --> 00:19:57,980
Because this is not accurate.

271
00:19:57,980 --> 00:19:59,500
Anybody who's met my dogs know.

272
00:19:59,500 --> 00:20:00,800
We're not there yet.

273
00:20:00,800 --> 00:20:03,380
But no human being can be tamed by the tongue.

274
00:20:03,380 --> 00:20:06,940
It is a restless evil full of deadly poison.

275
00:20:06,940 --> 00:20:08,620
Two parts of this.

276
00:20:08,740 --> 00:20:12,720
Number one, no human being can control their tongue.

277
00:20:12,720 --> 00:20:14,280
That's encouraging.

278
00:20:14,280 --> 00:20:19,460
Like, I'm reading this and I'm thinking, so James is giving us object illustration after object illustration.

279
00:20:19,460 --> 00:20:22,660
He's telling us the power and then he's saying, and you can't do anything about it.

280
00:20:22,660 --> 00:20:24,360
You can't control your tongue.

281
00:20:24,360 --> 00:20:26,980
He's right.

282
00:20:26,980 --> 00:20:28,220
We can't.

283
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:32,660
It's the power of Christ living in us that can.

284
00:20:32,660 --> 00:20:35,880
And that is one thing that I have realized through this.

285
00:20:35,880 --> 00:20:39,340
If we don't realize that, we will fall.

286
00:20:39,340 --> 00:20:40,440
We can try all we want.

287
00:20:40,440 --> 00:20:47,560
But it is through the power of Christ that's the only way that we have a shot of controlling what we say.

288
00:20:47,560 --> 00:20:51,320
And then it says, it is a restless evil full of deadly poison.

289
00:20:52,380 --> 00:20:56,120
There's a verse, I love Proverbs, the stuff in Proverbs, it never gets old.

290
00:20:56,120 --> 00:20:58,420
So there's a verse in Proverbs that really brings us to light.

291
00:20:58,420 --> 00:21:07,940
It says, somebody who doesn't consider the power of their words is like a maniac shooting flaming arrows of death.

292
00:21:07,940 --> 00:21:11,860
Is the one who deceives their neighbor and says, I was only joking.

293
00:21:11,860 --> 00:21:17,640
Have you ever been that sarcastic person when you say these mean dagger things and you're like, I'm just kidding.

294
00:21:17,640 --> 00:21:21,180
It's not a joke.

295
00:21:21,180 --> 00:21:22,540
They know it's not a joke.

296
00:21:22,540 --> 00:21:25,500
The words that you've said are shooting arrows of death.

297
00:21:25,500 --> 00:21:31,780
Apparently, saying I was only joking doesn't fix the damage that you've done.

298
00:21:31,780 --> 00:21:36,920
This is definitely a lesson that I have had to learn in my life over and over and over.

299
00:21:36,920 --> 00:21:40,140
Again, you might not have meant that.

300
00:21:40,140 --> 00:21:41,660
You may have had the greatest intentions.

301
00:21:41,660 --> 00:21:44,300
But we cannot see your intentions.

302
00:21:44,300 --> 00:21:48,200
And we cannot see the good heart that you say that you have.

303
00:21:48,200 --> 00:21:51,400
We only can hear the words that you give us.

304
00:21:51,400 --> 00:21:56,640
So, oh, we go to verse 9.

305
00:21:56,640 --> 00:22:00,100
It says, with the tongue, we praise our Lord and Father.

306
00:22:00,100 --> 00:22:04,340
And with it, we curse human beings who have been made in God's likeness.

307
00:22:04,740 --> 00:22:07,500
Out of the same mouth come praise and cursing.

308
00:22:07,500 --> 00:22:09,420
My brothers and sisters, this should not be.

309
00:22:09,420 --> 00:22:13,060
Can both fresh water and salt water flow from the same spring?

310
00:22:13,060 --> 00:22:18,240
My brothers and sisters, can a fig tree bear olives or a grapevine bear figs?

311
00:22:18,620 --> 00:22:21,440
Neither can a salt spring produce fresh water.

312
00:22:21,440 --> 00:22:24,740
My kids have the luxury of listening to me practice.

313
00:22:24,740 --> 00:22:29,280
And I was reading this verse, and they were like, what did you just say?

314
00:22:29,280 --> 00:22:30,340
That's a lot of words.

315
00:22:30,340 --> 00:22:40,860
But essentially, it's saying, you can't have Christ living in you, fully living in you, and running your life,

316
00:22:40,960 --> 00:22:45,300
and view others as anything but children of God, even if they've hurt you.

317
00:22:45,300 --> 00:22:47,900
They are a child of God in which God loves.

318
00:22:47,900 --> 00:22:56,200
And you can't have the fresh water of Jesus and then spew out salt water, which causes pain and singing.

319
00:22:56,780 --> 00:23:04,400
What he's saying is, if I'm really in you, then I should really be coming out of you in everything that you do.

320
00:23:04,400 --> 00:23:13,440
But the reality is, we think that we are filled with Christ, and oftentimes, we do spew salt water.

321
00:23:13,440 --> 00:23:16,560
We do produce the wrong fruit.

322
00:23:16,560 --> 00:23:21,280
So, what I've struggled with is why.

323
00:23:21,280 --> 00:23:24,740
Why is it so hard to control our words?

324
00:23:24,740 --> 00:23:26,500
Even James says it's so hard.

325
00:23:26,500 --> 00:23:33,920
So, one of the things that I realized is, for me, one of the reasons that I sometimes don't say the right words

326
00:23:33,920 --> 00:23:37,260
is because I feel like my words are justified.

327
00:23:37,260 --> 00:23:38,380
Has it felt like that?

328
00:23:38,380 --> 00:23:40,700
So, somebody hurt me.

329
00:23:40,700 --> 00:23:44,660
I am justified in hurting them back.

330
00:23:44,660 --> 00:23:49,720
Or, somebody did something wrong, and they hurt somebody.

331
00:23:49,720 --> 00:23:54,400
So, is it really wrong for me to tell all of you all the wrong things that they've done?

332
00:23:54,400 --> 00:23:55,880
Isn't that justified?

333
00:23:56,220 --> 00:23:57,340
Because they did it.

334
00:23:57,340 --> 00:24:01,060
So, they've gotten what they deserve.

335
00:24:01,060 --> 00:24:03,060
Not really doing anything wrong.

336
00:24:03,060 --> 00:24:07,840
Yet, those words are the spark that start a fire that destroy their lives.

337
00:24:08,420 --> 00:24:10,340
So, was it wrong or was it justified?

338
00:24:10,340 --> 00:24:13,620
This is something that I've realized that I struggle with.

339
00:24:13,620 --> 00:24:17,300
And, luckily for me, I'm not the only one who struggles with this.

340
00:24:17,300 --> 00:24:19,040
So, there was this king.

341
00:24:19,180 --> 00:24:20,180
His name was King Solomon.

342
00:24:20,180 --> 00:24:22,660
He was the son of King David.

343
00:24:22,660 --> 00:24:26,220
In my world, he's known as David and Goliath David.

344
00:24:26,220 --> 00:24:30,220
But, he actually grows up and becomes a king and he does some really big things.

345
00:24:30,220 --> 00:24:32,380
He's the man after God's own heart.

346
00:24:32,380 --> 00:24:37,520
So, Solomon becomes king in like this super easy way.

347
00:24:37,520 --> 00:24:40,320
So, his dad wins the battles.

348
00:24:40,320 --> 00:24:41,960
His dad builds up the kingdom.

349
00:24:42,400 --> 00:24:46,240
And so, when he becomes king, he's super rich, super powerful.

350
00:24:46,240 --> 00:24:50,440
And, he has a dream where God asks him, if I can give you anything, what would you want?

351
00:24:50,440 --> 00:24:51,420
He asks for wisdom.

352
00:24:51,860 --> 00:24:53,340
So, God gives him wisdom.

353
00:24:53,340 --> 00:24:56,640
So, he's known as the smartest man that ever lived, obviously, aside from Jesus.

354
00:24:56,640 --> 00:24:57,740
And, he's rich.

355
00:24:57,740 --> 00:24:58,980
And, he's powerful.

356
00:24:58,980 --> 00:25:01,560
So, what do you do when you're rich, powerful, and super smart?

357
00:25:01,560 --> 00:25:02,700
Journal.

358
00:25:02,700 --> 00:25:05,320
So, he did a lot of journaling.

359
00:25:05,320 --> 00:25:07,840
And, we get to read this journal.

360
00:25:07,840 --> 00:25:09,620
It's in Ecclesiastes.

361
00:25:09,620 --> 00:25:10,920
This is one of his journals.

362
00:25:10,920 --> 00:25:16,460
And, so, in this journal, he loses sleep with this idea of justice.

363
00:25:16,460 --> 00:25:17,860
He says, why?

364
00:25:17,860 --> 00:25:19,260
I'm prayer phrasing.

365
00:25:19,260 --> 00:25:19,940
I'll just read it.

366
00:25:19,940 --> 00:25:20,480
All right.

367
00:25:21,040 --> 00:25:26,800
Ecclesiastes 8.14 says, there's something else meaningless that occurs on earth.

368
00:25:26,800 --> 00:25:32,180
The righteous who get what the wicked deserve, and the wicked who get what the righteous deserve.

369
00:25:32,180 --> 00:25:35,480
So, he's watching this happen time and time again.

370
00:25:35,480 --> 00:25:40,060
That the righteous people aren't getting what they deserve, and the wicked people aren't getting what they deserve.

371
00:25:40,060 --> 00:25:45,540
You can probably all think of somebody right now who does not deserve what they are getting.

372
00:25:45,640 --> 00:25:51,160
Whether they have lived their lives and followed God, and they have a terminal cancer.

373
00:25:51,160 --> 00:25:52,040
And, you're like, really?

374
00:25:52,040 --> 00:25:57,980
Where you have that person that is just time and time again running people over and treating them like garbage.

375
00:25:57,980 --> 00:25:59,340
Yet, they keep getting promoted.

376
00:25:59,340 --> 00:26:01,240
And, their house is bigger than yours.

377
00:26:01,240 --> 00:26:03,140
And, their kids are better behaved than yours.

378
00:26:03,140 --> 00:26:05,140
And, it's, you just don't get it.

379
00:26:05,200 --> 00:26:08,680
Like, why are the righteous not getting what the righteous deserve?

380
00:26:08,680 --> 00:26:10,420
And, he struggles with this.

381
00:26:10,960 --> 00:26:13,040
In, Ecclesiastes 3.10, he says,

382
00:26:13,040 --> 00:26:16,300
I have seen the burden that God has laid on the human race.

383
00:26:16,300 --> 00:26:19,740
He has made everything beautiful in its time.

384
00:26:19,740 --> 00:26:23,280
He has also set eternity in the human heart.

385
00:26:23,280 --> 00:26:27,160
Yet, no one can fathom what God has done from beginning to end.

386
00:26:27,160 --> 00:26:32,300
He's starting to get a little bit of what's going on.

387
00:26:32,300 --> 00:26:35,820
He says, God made everything beautiful in its time.

388
00:26:35,820 --> 00:26:37,800
But, it's not time yet.

389
00:26:38,440 --> 00:26:41,800
He says, that God has set eternity in the human heart.

390
00:26:41,800 --> 00:26:47,300
Eternity, that, the other side of this, when we get to heaven,

391
00:26:47,300 --> 00:26:54,780
that is when Solomon is realizing that true justification is obtained.

392
00:26:54,780 --> 00:27:02,300
True fairness will come to light on the other side when we get to heaven.

393
00:27:02,300 --> 00:27:09,200
And, he's starting to realize that we can't understand what God is doing.

394
00:27:09,200 --> 00:27:11,560
This is something that's hard to wrap our heads around.

395
00:27:11,560 --> 00:27:13,660
But, we don't know what we don't know.

396
00:27:13,660 --> 00:27:14,740
But, God does.

397
00:27:14,740 --> 00:27:19,920
And, even if we think he didn't see what that person did to us, he saw it all.

398
00:27:19,920 --> 00:27:25,220
And, he tells us, I will make it right in my time.

399
00:27:26,300 --> 00:27:33,220
C.S. Lewis, actually, he's famous for mere Christianity, Chronicles of Narnia, Problem of Pain.

400
00:27:33,220 --> 00:27:33,960
He's very famous.

401
00:27:33,960 --> 00:27:35,680
He starts out as an atheist.

402
00:27:35,680 --> 00:27:41,960
But, it's this idea of justice that actually brings him to Christianity.

403
00:27:41,960 --> 00:27:48,540
He says, my argument against God was that the universe seems so cruel and unjust.

404
00:27:48,540 --> 00:27:50,460
I've heard this argument so many times.

405
00:27:50,520 --> 00:27:53,740
How can there be a God if the world is so cruel and unjust?

406
00:27:53,740 --> 00:27:54,760
What type of God is that?

407
00:27:54,760 --> 00:28:00,120
But, how had I got this idea of just and unjust?

408
00:28:00,120 --> 00:28:04,340
A man does not call a line crooked unless he has some idea of a straight line.

409
00:28:04,340 --> 00:28:08,580
What was I comparing this universe with when I called it unjust?

410
00:28:08,580 --> 00:28:11,940
So, in other words, I'm sinful.

411
00:28:11,940 --> 00:28:13,100
I know that I mess up.

412
00:28:13,100 --> 00:28:16,380
But, my idea of right is skewed towards myself.

413
00:28:16,500 --> 00:28:21,360
So, there has to be an ultimate line, an ultimate right versus wrong.

414
00:28:21,360 --> 00:28:28,000
And, if there is that, and it's none of us because we're all screwed up and selfish, there has to be someone over us.

415
00:28:28,000 --> 00:28:37,220
So, he starts to realize this idea of justice that I have in my head, this idea that I want fairness, came from someone higher than me.

416
00:28:37,220 --> 00:28:40,240
And so, he starts to look into Christianity.

417
00:28:41,940 --> 00:28:45,020
Ecclesiastes 3.17, Solomon says,

418
00:28:45,020 --> 00:28:51,960
I said to myself, God will bring unto judgment both the justice and the wicked, both the righteous and the wicked.

419
00:28:51,960 --> 00:28:56,080
And there will be a time for every activity, a time to judge every deed.

420
00:28:56,080 --> 00:29:02,120
Yes, this is the verse where the Beatles got their famous song, A Season, Everything, There Is A Season, I think it's called.

421
00:29:02,900 --> 00:29:09,540
But, he's saying that the bottom line is, I don't get what I don't get, but it's God's timing.

422
00:29:09,540 --> 00:29:18,200
And it's, I have to accept the fact that he will bring everything to its right place at his time.

423
00:29:18,200 --> 00:29:21,500
The reality is, is you and I are not gods.

424
00:29:21,500 --> 00:29:24,300
We think we are gods.

425
00:29:24,300 --> 00:29:24,800
We do.

426
00:29:24,800 --> 00:29:25,640
We really do.

427
00:29:25,640 --> 00:29:28,240
Because we think that everything should go the way we want it to go.

428
00:29:28,680 --> 00:29:30,140
Every one of us thinks that.

429
00:29:30,140 --> 00:29:31,520
But we are not gods.

430
00:29:31,520 --> 00:29:33,540
And we have to remember this.

431
00:29:33,540 --> 00:29:38,200
Solomon talks about the fact that, this is, this is kind of funny to me, but we were made from dust.

432
00:29:38,200 --> 00:29:41,540
So, he goes on to explain, you are made from dust.

433
00:29:41,540 --> 00:29:42,920
You know what else we're made from dust?

434
00:29:42,920 --> 00:29:43,560
Cows.

435
00:29:43,560 --> 00:29:46,180
You and cows came from the same origin.

436
00:29:46,180 --> 00:29:48,160
So, you will die.

437
00:29:48,160 --> 00:29:50,180
And your body will go in a hole.

438
00:29:50,180 --> 00:29:53,180
And you will fertilize the flowers.

439
00:29:53,800 --> 00:29:55,660
And then the cow will eat the flowers.

440
00:29:55,660 --> 00:29:58,000
And then humans will eat the cow.

441
00:29:58,000 --> 00:29:59,860
And then they will die.

442
00:29:59,860 --> 00:30:03,800
And their bodies will go as fertilizer, which will grow the flowers.

443
00:30:03,800 --> 00:30:07,560
And he's basically saying, don't think of yourself more highly than you are.

444
00:30:07,560 --> 00:30:08,800
You are but dust.

445
00:30:08,800 --> 00:30:12,520
This doesn't mean that God doesn't love us, because he says, you're precious in my sight.

446
00:30:12,520 --> 00:30:14,340
And he knows every hair on your head.

447
00:30:14,340 --> 00:30:15,620
And he forms you in your mother's womb.

448
00:30:15,620 --> 00:30:21,220
But what he's saying is, don't think you are more powerful than you are.

449
00:30:21,760 --> 00:30:25,400
Romans 12 says, do not repay evil back for evil.

450
00:30:25,400 --> 00:30:28,760
Do not take revenge, my dear friends, but leave room for God's wrath.

451
00:30:28,760 --> 00:30:31,500
For it is written, it is mine to avenge.

452
00:30:31,500 --> 00:30:32,740
I will repay.

453
00:30:32,740 --> 00:30:43,100
As I was writing this, I was thinking, I don't know what thing has happened to you that has caused you to want to repay evil back for evil.

454
00:30:43,100 --> 00:30:46,740
But I do know that God saw every single step of it.

455
00:30:46,740 --> 00:30:48,560
I know that he knew it was coming.

456
00:30:48,560 --> 00:30:51,440
