518
00:34:24,340 --> 00:34:25,780
It's not easy.

519
00:34:26,360 --> 00:34:27,520
Not even close.

520
00:34:27,520 --> 00:34:32,200
But again, we aren't doing it in our own power.

521
00:34:32,200 --> 00:34:33,320
We can't.

522
00:34:33,320 --> 00:34:35,960
Because we will overcome evil with evil.

523
00:34:35,960 --> 00:34:36,980
We will.

524
00:34:36,980 --> 00:34:38,200
That's what we want to do.

525
00:34:38,200 --> 00:34:40,600
So we can't do it in our own power.

526
00:34:40,600 --> 00:34:47,020
This next verse is one thing that I have been trying to live day in and day out.

527
00:34:47,020 --> 00:34:48,860
2 Corinthians 5, 16 says,

528
00:34:48,860 --> 00:34:52,760
From now on we regard no one from an earthly view.

529
00:34:53,720 --> 00:34:56,740
We have to see people through the eyes of Jesus.

530
00:34:56,740 --> 00:34:58,680
This is not easy.

531
00:34:58,680 --> 00:35:03,400
This reminds me of, I talked like literally years or two years ago or something about,

532
00:35:03,400 --> 00:35:08,040
if you have that tape that plays over and over in your head that tells you the negative thoughts,

533
00:35:08,040 --> 00:35:11,100
you have to cognitively stop that tape.

534
00:35:11,100 --> 00:35:12,660
You have to pause the tape.

535
00:35:12,660 --> 00:35:13,880
Nope, I'm not going to believe that.

536
00:35:13,880 --> 00:35:14,640
I'm not going to believe it.

537
00:35:14,640 --> 00:35:17,100
And give yourself positive words of God.

538
00:35:17,200 --> 00:35:18,920
It's a practice that you do over and over again.

539
00:35:18,920 --> 00:35:20,180
So is this.

540
00:35:20,180 --> 00:35:25,840
When you see that person that you can't stand or somebody does something that is mean,

541
00:35:25,840 --> 00:35:29,700
you have to cognitively stop the negative thought.

542
00:35:29,700 --> 00:35:31,460
I've been practicing this.

543
00:35:31,460 --> 00:35:32,120
It's not easy.

544
00:35:32,120 --> 00:35:32,860
But it does.

545
00:35:32,860 --> 00:35:38,600
You have to train your brain to view them through the eyes of Jesus, not through our eyes.

546
00:35:38,600 --> 00:35:49,100
The best illustration that I can give is, as a mom, as moms out there, we see our children through very different eyes than the rest of the world, right?

547
00:35:49,320 --> 00:35:54,340
When they're screaming and losing their minds at Target, and everyone else is like, what a brat.

548
00:35:54,340 --> 00:35:56,660
My mind is, they're hungry.

549
00:35:56,660 --> 00:35:57,900
They didn't get their nap.

550
00:35:57,900 --> 00:35:59,260
They're tired.

551
00:35:59,260 --> 00:36:00,760
Like, it's okay.

552
00:36:00,760 --> 00:36:02,440
I promise they're a good person.

553
00:36:02,440 --> 00:36:04,280
Those are the eyes we need to see other people.

554
00:36:04,280 --> 00:36:11,600
Through the eyes of a mother who loves their child and knows their child and wants the best for their child and wants you to view them.

555
00:36:11,600 --> 00:36:13,640
That's how Jesus views us.

556
00:36:13,640 --> 00:36:17,360
And that's how he asks us to view others.

557
00:36:17,360 --> 00:36:18,660
It's through his eyes.

558
00:36:18,660 --> 00:36:21,420
He died for them just like he died for us.

559
00:36:21,420 --> 00:36:22,800
And he loves them.

560
00:36:22,800 --> 00:36:26,920
No matter what they're doing to us, he loves them so much.

